module b3;

<*
 A joint known to be a mover joint, so its per-type accessors need no check at each call. It
 converts to a JointId on its own, so every shared accessor reaches it uncast; the way back is
 JointId.as_mover(), which checks — see there for what a wrong-typed accessor does.
*>
typedef MoverJointId = inline JointId;

<*
 A mover joint definition: drives a dynamic character body towards linear_velocity with at most
 max_force newtons, applied only in the xz plane of local frame B. It does not affect rotation.
 Must come from default_mover_joint_def(), which zeroes both fields, so a default mover drives
 nothing. box3d's assertion that max_force is finite and at or above 0 is compiled out here.
*>
struct MoverJointDef {
    inline JointDef base;
    Vec3 linear_velocity;
    float max_force;
}

extern fn MoverJointDef default_mover_joint_def() @cname("b3DefaultMoverJointDef");

<*
 Raw mover joint constructor. Bypasses create_mover_joint's definition guard and hands back a
 joint of no particular type, so it is private to the module — src/joint_mover.c3's
 create_mover_joint is the only caller and is the only public way to a live mover joint.
*>
extern fn JointId create_mover_joint_raw(
  WorldId world_id,
  MoverJointDef* def,
) @cname("b3CreateMoverJoint") @private;

<*
 Sets the velocity of body B relative to body A that the joint drives towards, in metres per
 second along the world axes. Only its projection on local frame B's x and z axes is driven, as
 those axes stand on body B now, so the component along frame B's y axis is ignored. Asserted
 finite under an assertion this build compiles out. The accumulated impulse stands.
*>
extern fn void MoverJointId.set_linear_velocity(self, Vec3 velocity) @cname("b3MoverJoint_SetLinearVelocity");

<*
 The velocity the joint drives body B towards relative to body A, in world axes. What was set,
 including any component the joint ignores, not what the bodies are doing. Zero on a joint built
 from a default definition.
*>
extern fn Vec3 MoverJointId.linear_velocity(self) @cname("b3MoverJoint_GetLinearVelocity");

<*
 Sets the ceiling in newtons on the planar force the drive may apply. 0, a default definition's
 value, drives nothing and cancels the impulse the drive held. Asserted finite and at or above 0
 under an assertion this build compiles out: a negative is stored, acts as its magnitude until the
 drive saturates, and then pushes away from the target.
*>
extern fn void MoverJointId.set_max_velocity_force(self, float max_force) @cname("b3MoverJoint_SetMaxVelocityForce");

<*
 The ceiling in newtons on the planar force the drive may apply. MoverJointDef names it max_force.
 0 on a joint built from a default definition.
*>
extern fn float MoverJointId.max_velocity_force(self) @cname("b3MoverJoint_GetMaxVelocityForce");
